.SH NAME
.PP
ziptime \- zip timestamp tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
To normalize the timestamps in the Zip header:
.PP
\f[B]ziptime\f[] \f[I]file.zip\f[]
.PP
where \f[I]file.zip\f[] is an existing Zip archive to rewrite.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This tools replaces the timestamps in the zip headers with a static time
(Jan 1 2008).
The extra fields are not changed, so you'll need to use the \-X option
to zip so that it doesn't create the `universal time' extra.
